+# Host tests for the Android media backend
+
+The pure logic of the backend (buffering, MIME table, YUV packing) is
+host-testable. This harness compiles the exact shipped files on the host via
+#[path] includes and runs their unit tests. The NDK-dependent code
+(sys.rs/source.rs/player.rs) is compiled only for Android targets.
+
+## Invocation
+
+    cd components/media/backends/android/hosttest
+    cargo test
+
+Requires any stable Rust toolchain (verified with 1.99.1). No Servo checkout,
+no Android SDK/NDK needed. The own [workspace] in Cargo.toml keeps this out of
+the Servo workspace when the crate is vendored into it.
+
+## Results (2026-11-06)
+
+    test result: ok. 13 passed; 0 failed
+
+Covered: SharedBuffer windows/seeks (6), mime_table answers (3),
+yuv_pack packing incl. row/pixel strides (4). NOT covered (need device
+evidence): codec format negotiation, crop/rotation/color changes, odd
+dimensions, ImageReader-decoder compatibility, A/V sync, audio focus/routes.
